erver/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/deployments","created_at":"2026-01-19T08:04:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T09:05:37Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-06T11:52:44Z","git_url":"git://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:m2ux/workflow-server.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server","homepage":"","size":69436,"stargazers_count":2,"watchers_count":2,"language":"TypeScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":1,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":126,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":1,"open_issues":126,"watchers":2,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"body":"## Overview\n\nWork Planner leaves failed readiness and merge attempts in an explicit, verified state. Hot-fix review failure withdraws ready state, and epic integration follows the owning merge result without unintended retries or success assertions.\n\n## Problem\n\n- Hot-fix readiness can fail after marking a pull request ready, while the repair route promises draft state without an explicit restoring write and readback.\n- Epic integration treats refusal generically although the owning merge operation distinguishes harness denial and GitHub refusal, and its final readback assumes a merge.\n- The task merge command omits the verified head SHA, so a head moving between verification and the mutation can merge unverified content.\n- The merge-permission field describes task-to-epic-base authorization while the shared operation handles further delivery targets.\n\n## Proposal\n\nDeliver Mode selects the existing draft command and confirms its result before hot-fix repair. Pull Request owns explicit merge outcomes and the permission boundary; Epic Integration consumes them with bounded retry and terminal handoff/refusal branches. One atomic unit changes the shared merge contract and its epic caller. The task merge mutation includes its verified head SHA; a mismatch supplies refusal evidence for fresh verification within the existing retry bound. Behavior is verified with ordered calls and terminal-result fixtures, including restoration failure and each refusal source.\n\n## Work Breakdown\n\n| Task | Description | Coverage | Depends on | Joins | Lane | Done |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [W01](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1657) | Confirm draft state after failed hot-fix readiness | AC1, AC2, AC3 | [E01:W08](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/1616) | | | ✓ |\n| [W02](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1658) | Explicit merge outcomes and permission boundaries | AC4, AC5, AC8 | [E01:W08](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/1616) | W03 | | ✓ |\n| [W03](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/pull/1658) | Epic continuation follows the merge outcome | AC6, AC7 | [E01:W08](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/1616) | W02 | | ✓ |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] **AC1.** A hot-fix validation failure after a ready write selects draft restoration and confirms current draft state before repair, as ordered failure-route fixtures show.\n- [x] **AC2.** A failed restoration or disagreeing readback produces an explicit unresolved discrepancy without claiming draft state or reaching merge/In Review, as negative fixtures show.\n- [x] **AC3.** Passing hot-fix review and ready readback reaches normal merge exactly once, as a positive route fixture shows.\n- [x] **AC4.** Merge Delivery Pull Request provides distinct confirmed-merge, human-handoff, harness-denial and GitHub-refusal outcomes with current head/target evidence, as contract and outcome fixtures show.\n- [x] **AC5.** Merge Permission describes the existing authorization/capability boundary for each supported delivery target without authorizing protection bypass or widening harness permission, as source review against configured target requirements and permission-denial fixtures shows.\n- [x] **AC6.** Epic integration terminates human handoff and harness denial without same-run retry or merged-success readback, as ordered negative fixtures show.\n- [x] **AC7.** Epic integration retries GitHub refusal only within the existing bound after fresh verification, terminates repeated refusal, and confirms merged head/target/commit only after a confirmed merge, as route fixtures show.\n\n- [x] **AC8.** The task merge mutation includes the verified head SHA and refuses a moved head without a success claim or unchecked retry, as captured-request and moving-head refusal fixtures show.\n\n## References\n\n- **R1.** [Recovery design](https://github.com/m2ux/workflow-server/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-06-1597-delivery-failure-recovery/design.md) — source evidence, ownership, units and regression matrix.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/1654/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/workflow-server/issues/1654/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null},"content_type":"Issue","creator":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-06T08:10:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T11:51:42Z","archived_at":null,"item_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/projectsV2/17/items/295717376","fields":[{"id":422017304,"name":"Status","data_type":"single_select","value":{"id":"98236657","name":{"raw":"Done","html":"Done"},"description":{"raw":"Closed or merged","html":"Closed or merged"},"color":"GREEN"}}]}
